Subject: lottie: a slot applied on the same frame refreshes the layers' transforms

LottieBuilder::updateTransform() caches each layer's matrix and opacity by frame number
(layer->cache.frameNo) and returns early when asked for the same frame. A slot that overrides a
layer's transform (opacity, position...) and is applied without a frame change sets `build`, and
sync() rebuilds the scene, but every layer still returns its cached matrix and opacity from
before the slot: the override shows only from the next frame on. Seen with layers switched by a
slot on their opacity (Lordicon's legacy per-width stroke layers): changing the stroke of a
paused icon drew the old width.

The builder now keeps a generation, bumped when sync() rebuilds for a slot, and a layer's cache
holds only for the generation it was computed in.

Origin: Lordicon.
Base: thorvg/thorvg main 72a66415 (1.2.0). License: MIT, like ThorVG.
---
--- a/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieModel.h
+++ b/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieModel.h
@@ -1162,6 +1162,7 @@
 
     struct {
         float frameNo = -1.0f;
+        uint32_t gen = 0;  //builder generation the cache was computed in (slots applied since)
         Matrix matrix;
         uint8_t opacity;
     } cache;
--- a/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieBuilder.h
+++ b/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieBuilder.h
@@ -178,6 +178,7 @@
     const AssetResolver* resolver = nullptr;  //do not free this
     AudioResolver audioResolver;
     LottieTween tween;
+    uint32_t gen = 0;  //bumped when slots change the model without a frame change
     float volume = 1.0f;
 
 private:
--- a/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieBuilder.cpp
+++ b/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieBuilder.cpp
@@ -183,8 +183,9 @@
     if (tween.active) {
         layer->cache.frameNo = -1.0f;  // tweening doesn't cache the result; invalidate it
     } else {
-        if (tvg::equal(layer->cache.frameNo, frameNo)) return;
+        if (tvg::equal(layer->cache.frameNo, frameNo) && layer->cache.gen == gen) return;
         layer->cache.frameNo = frameNo;
+        layer->cache.gen = gen;
     }
 
     auto transform = layer->transform;
--- a/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieLoader.cpp
+++ b/src/loaders/lottie/tvgLottieLoader.cpp
@@ -433,6 +433,8 @@
 
     if (build) {
         if (comp) comp->clear();
+        //A slot changed the model on the same frame: the layers' cached transforms are stale.
+        ++builder->gen;
         run(0);
     }
     return true;
